      "heading": "Fergus is a solid job manager",
      "text": "We are not going to pretend Fergus is bad. It is a well-liked job-management tool built for trades: quoting, job tracking, scheduling, timesheets and invoicing, with a clear focus on the financial health of each job. If you run a trades business and need to manage quotes, jobs and invoices in one place, Fergus is built for exactly that and does it well. Quickler is a different category. It does not quote or invoice and it is not trying to. It is the lightweight, no-app layer that captures inspections and compliance records on site, in WhatsApp. If you need job and invoice management, Fergus is the right tool. If you just need inspections captured without an app, that is us."
