  "articlePanels": [{"kind":"lede","html":"<p>Fergus is a job, quote and invoice management tool for trades. So the honest reason to look for a <strong>fergus alternative uk</strong> teams will use is usually not that Fergus is weak. It is that Fergus manages jobs and money, and some teams do not need that. They need inspections and compliance captured on site.</p><p>Here is a fair comparison, where Fergus is the right choice, and where a no-app capture layer wins.</p>"},{"kind":"takeaways","heading":"The short version","html":"<ul><li>Fergus is a well-liked job-management tool for trades: quoting, job tracking, scheduling, timesheets, invoicing, with job profitability built in. Pricing is a per-user subscription.</li><li>If you need to manage quotes, jobs and invoices in one place, Fergus is the right category and does it well. We say that plainly.</li><li>Quickler is not a smaller, cheaper Fergus. It is a different category: the no-app layer that captures inspections and compliance records on site.</li><li>Quickler runs in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat. No app, no login.</li><li>Quickler is £20 per active user a month, dormant users free, only pay for who works, everything unlimited on a paid account.</li><li>Pricing figures for Fergus are approximate. Check their current pricing before deciding.</li></ul>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"Credit where due","heading":"What Fergus does well","html":"<p>An honest comparison starts where the product is strong, and Fergus is strong at what it sets out to do.</p><p>It is built around the job and the money on it. Quoting and estimating, a clear job status board, scheduling, timesheets and invoicing all live together, and the standout feature is how visibly it tracks profitability on each job. For a trades business that wants to stop losing margin to admin and half-finished quotes, that focus is genuinely useful.</p><p>The interface is approachable and the tool is aimed squarely at small and growing trades firms rather than large enterprises, which suits its market. If you run a plumbing, electrical or building business and need to manage jobs and cash flow, Fergus is a sensible, capable choice. None of that is in doubt.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The real difference","heading":"It is a job manager, not a capture layer","html":"<p>The difference between Fergus and Quickler is not that one is better. It is that they are different categories. Fergus manages jobs and invoicing. Quickler captures one thing well: inspections and compliance records, on site, without an app.</p><p>Fergus has a mobile app for field staff, as job-management tools do. It carries job details, times and notes, which is useful, but it is still an app to open and a login to keep alive. For inspection and compliance capture specifically, that is the same on-site friction any app has. The check gets done, the app gets filled in later from memory, and the record reflects what someone remembered.</p><p>Quickler does not try to replace job or invoice management. If that is what you need, Fergus is the right answer and a capture layer will not stand in for it. Quickler solves the narrower problem of getting the on-site inspection record captured reliably in the first place.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The alternatives","heading":"Job managers, paper, and WhatsApp","html":"<p><strong>Fergus</strong> is the job-and-money tool done well: quote, track, schedule, invoice, with profitability built in. Pick it when you need to manage jobs and cash flow, not just inspections. It is the right category for that job.</p><p><strong>Paper and spreadsheets</strong> stay common in UK teams. Free, familiar, no training. The records are illegible, unsearchable, and impossible to produce when a client or regulator asks. The cost is not the subscription. It is the liability when the folder cannot be found.</p><p><strong>Quickler</strong> removes the app for the capture step. The inspection workflow arrives in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat and they reply to each question as a message. Same behaviour they already do all day, no install, no login. The tradeoff is that quickler is not a job or invoice manager and does not try to be.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The no-app option","heading":"Quickler, and where it stops","html":"<p>Quickler runs in WhatsApp. Nothing to install, no login. The inspection or compliance workflow arrives in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat, and they reply to each question as a message. Voice notes are transcribed automatically. The core output is a shareable web report and a permanent record, with optional PDF and CSV export. Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you add your whole team and only pay for who actually works. Everything is unlimited on a paid account, so anyone who reads but never files adds nothing to the cost.</p><p>The honest limit: quickler is not job-management or invoicing software. It does not quote, track job profit, schedule or invoice. If you need any of that, Fergus is the more complete product for the job and there is no contest. Quickler is built for teams of roughly 1 to 30 doing structured compliance and inspection capture. It serves care homes, nurseries, schools, estates, cleaning firms and trades, anyone who inspects or keeps records. Rooted in UK compliance, it works anywhere WhatsApp does. If you need to manage jobs and invoices, Fergus is the right tool. If you just need the on-site record captured, that is what quickler does.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"Scope, install, price","heading":"Direct comparison","html":"<table><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Scope</th><th>App install?</th><th>Pricing model</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fergus</td><td>Job, quote and invoice management</td><td>Yes, login required</td><td>Per user subscription</td></tr><tr><td>SimPro</td><td>Full job management and FSM</td><td>Yes, login required</td><td>Quote-based, platform tier</td></tr><tr><td>Joblogic</td><td>Full field-service management</td><td>Yes, login required</td><td>Per user, quote-based</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Quickler</strong></td><td><strong>Inspection and compliance capture</strong></td><td><strong>No, WhatsApp only</strong></td><td><strong>£20 per active user/mo, dormant users free</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Pricing is approximate. Check each vendor's current pricing before deciding. The deciding test is simple: do you need to manage jobs and invoices, or just capture inspections reliably on site? If the former, Fergus is the right category. If the latter, a WhatsApp-native workflow removes the app barrier because your team already uses WhatsApp. See <a href=\"/pages/simpro-alternative-uk.html\">SimPro alternative UK</a> and <a href=\"/pages/joblogic-alternative-uk.html\">Joblogic alternative UK</a>.</p>"},{"kind":"faq","heading":"Questions, answered","html":"<h3>Is Fergus any good?</h3><p>Yes. Fergus is a well-liked job-management tool for trades, covering quoting, job tracking, scheduling, timesheets and invoicing, with job profitability built in. If you need to manage jobs and cash flow in one place, it is a sensible, capable choice. We would not tell you otherwise.</p><h3>What is the difference between Fergus and Quickler?</h3><p>They are different categories. Fergus is a job, quote and invoice manager that tracks the money on each job. Quickler is a lightweight capture layer that gets inspections and compliance records captured on site, in WhatsApp, with no app and no login. Quickler does not quote or invoice and is not trying to replace Fergus.</p><h3>Is Quickler cheaper than Fergus?</h3><p>They are not really comparable on price because they do different jobs. Fergus is a per-user job-management subscription. Quickler charges £20 per active user a month, where an active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, and dormant users are free. If all you need is inspection capture, quickler is lighter and cheaper. If you need job and invoice management, Fergus is doing a different job for the money.</p><h3>Should I switch from Fergus to Quickler?</h3><p>Usually not as a straight swap, because they do different things. If you rely on Fergus for quotes, jobs and invoices, keep it. Many teams add quickler alongside it purely for on-site inspection and compliance capture, so the record gets caught reliably without another app. Quickler has a free tier of 20 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock. Related: <a href=\"/pages/joblogic-alternative-uk.html\">Joblogic alternative UK</a> and <a href=\"/pages/alternatives.html\">all comparisons</a>.</p>"}],
