  "seoBody": "<h2>Is Fergus a good product?</h2><p>Yes. We will say that plainly. Fergus is a well-liked job-management tool for trades. Quoting, job tracking, scheduling, timesheets and invoicing all live together, and it is built around the profitability of each job, which is a genuinely useful focus for a trades business trying to stop losing margin to admin.</p><p>So the honest reason firms go looking for a Fergus alternative is rarely that Fergus is weak. It is that Fergus manages jobs and money, and some teams do not need that. They need inspections and compliance captured reliably on site.</p><h2>The real difference</h2><p>Fergus and Quickler are different categories. Fergus manages jobs and invoicing. Quickler captures one thing well: inspections and compliance records, on site, without an app.</p><p>Fergus has a mobile app for field staff, as job-management tools do, carrying job details and times. For inspection capture specifically, that is still an app to open and a login to keep alive. The check gets done, the app gets filled in later from memory, and the record reflects what someone remembered rather than what they observed.</p><p>Quickler does not try to replace job or invoice management. If that is what you need, Fergus is the right answer and a capture layer will not stand in for it.</p><h2>The alternatives</h2><h3>Fergus</h3><p>The job-and-money tool done well: quote, track, schedule, invoice, with profitability built in. Pick it when you need to manage jobs and cash flow, not just inspections. It is the right category for that job.</p><h3>Paper and spreadsheets</h3><p>Still common in UK teams. Free, familiar, no training. The records are illegible, unsearchable, and impossible to produce when a client or regulator asks. The cost is not the subscription. It is the liability when the folder cannot be found.</p><h3>Quickler</h3><p>Quickler runs in WhatsApp. There is nothing to install and no login. The inspection or compliance workflow arrives in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat, and they reply to each question as a message, the same way they reply to anything else. Voice notes are transcribed automatically. The core output is a shareable web report and a permanent record, with optional PDF and CSV export.</p><p>Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you add your whole team and only pay for who actually works. Everything is unlimited on a paid account.</p><p>The honest limitation: quickler is not job-management or invoicing software. It does not quote, track job profit, schedule or invoice. For any of that, Fergus is the more complete product for the job. Quickler is built for teams of roughly 1 to 30 doing structured compliance and inspection capture, and it serves care homes, nurseries, schools, estates, cleaning firms and trades, anyone who inspects or keeps records. Rooted in UK compliance, it works anywhere WhatsApp does.</p><h2>Direct comparison</h2><p><strong>Fergus:</strong> job, quote and invoice management; app install and login required; per-user subscription.</p><p><strong>SimPro:</strong> full job management and FSM; app install and login required; quote-based pricing at the platform tier.</p><p><strong>Joblogic:</strong> full field-service management; app install and login required; per-user, quote-based.</p><p><strong>Quickler:</strong> inspection and compliance capture; £20 per active user/mo, dormant users free, only pay for who works; WhatsApp only, no install; UK-based, direct founder contact.</p><p>Pricing is approximate. Check each vendor's current pricing before deciding.</p><h2>How to choose</h2><p>The deciding test is simple: do you need to manage jobs and invoices, or just capture inspections reliably on site?</p><p>If you need to quote, track and invoice jobs and see the profit on each one, Fergus is the right category and a capture layer will not replace it.</p><p>If your problem is narrower, that inspections and compliance checks are not being captured reliably because opening an app on site is one step too many, a WhatsApp-native workflow removes the barrier because your team already uses WhatsApp for everything else.</p><p><strong>One thing to check before deciding:</strong> many teams run both, a job manager for the money and quickler for the on-site record. They are not mutually exclusive.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is Fergus any good?</h3><p>Yes. Fergus is a well-liked job-management tool for trades, covering quoting, job tracking, scheduling, timesheets and invoicing, with job profitability built in. If you need to manage jobs and cash flow in one place, it is a sensible, capable choice.</p><h3>What is the difference between Fergus and Quickler?</h3><p>They are different categories. Fergus is a job, quote and invoice manager that tracks the money on each job. Quickler is a lightweight capture layer that gets inspections and compliance records captured on site, in WhatsApp, with no app and no login. Quickler does not quote or invoice.</p><h3>Is Quickler cheaper than Fergus?</h3><p>They are not really comparable on price because they do different jobs. Fergus is a per-user job-management subscription. Quickler charges £20 per active user a month, where an active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, and dormant users are free. If all you need is inspection capture, quickler is lighter and cheaper. If you need job and invoice management, Fergus is doing a different job.</p><h3>Should I switch from Fergus to Quickler?</h3><p>Usually not as a straight swap, because they do different things. If you rely on Fergus for quotes, jobs and invoices, keep it. Many teams add quickler alongside it purely for on-site inspection and compliance capture. Quickler has a free tier of 20 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p><h2>Try this in Quickler</h2><p>Start free, no card, no trial clock. Copy and paste this into the workflow description when you sign up at <a href=\"https://app.quickler.co/signup\">app.quickler.co/signup</a>:</p><p><code>Fergus alternative for inspection capture. Workflow name: [Your inspection or compliance check name]. Description: Describe the on-site check you need captured. Include: what is being inspected, number of questions, whether photos are required, and what the output looks like. Quickler builds it as a WhatsApp workflow. £20 per active user a month, dormant users free, only pay for who works.</code></p><p>Quickler reads your description and builds the WhatsApp question sequence. Your team answers on site. Report produced automatically.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/simpro-alternative-uk.html\">SimPro alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/joblogic-alternative-uk.html\">Joblogic alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/fieldwire-alternative-uk.html\">Fieldwire alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/alternatives.html\">All comparisons</a></li></ul>",
